keywords:
  - control-theory
  - bayesian-inference
  - signal-processing
  - adaptive-control
  - phase-lead-compensator
  - zero-lag-filtering
abstract: >-
  The Dynamic Decision Algorithm (DDA) is a recursive control framework that solves the "Inertia Paradox" in sequential decision-making. 
  By decoupling phase-lag reduction from noise rejection via a pre-cognitive unity-gain update law, DDA achieves zero-lag tracking 
  in non-stationary environments while maintaining stability in high-noise regimes. Validated against optimized EMA baselines 
  with >25% improvement in tracking error.